  "title": "2026-07-25-eval-160035 · eval-harness-orchestration",
  "description": "# Offline evaluation harness orchestration\nA left-to-right, top-to-bottom flow showing how a pinned, fingerprinted scenario suite is executed by a bounded worker pool against an isolated system under test; how infrastructure faults remain distinct from product regressions; and how independent evidence-backed graders produce a scorecard for fingerprint-compatible comparison. Comparable-run swings trigger scenario re-runs under a bounded retry allowance. Attempt variance is retained, and results that remain unstable are explicitly marked unstable rather than averaged. Artifacts, transcripts, verdicts, and variance remain auditable, while a promoted compatible run becomes a future baseline.",
  "mode": "diagram",
